## View: AutomationDetails

### Summary

An opened automation: its details on the left, its recipients on the right.

### Display

- Name, Event, Channel and Content, read for any signed-in staff member — [reads](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [reads](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Content), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Requirements[AUTODETAILS]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[SESSIONONLY])
- The content choice offers only the organisation's contents — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMORG])

### Actions

- Save — [exposes](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Operation:UpdateCommunication)
- Recipients — [navigates](aim:juicebar.communications.recipients#View:AutomationRecipients)

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/automation/automation-details/automation-details.component.ts#AutomationDetailsComponent` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#getCommunication` — as: handler
- binds: `service:communication-service#searchContents` — as: handler
- binds: `service:communication-service#getContent` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: CreateCommunication

### Summary

A staff member creates an automation with its name, event and channel.

### Input

```schema
name: string required
event: string
channel: string required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.core#Persona:Staff`

### Ensures

- An automation exists in the staff member's organisation with the name, the event and the channel, run 0 times, active only for the events Manual communication and Scheduled communications — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Requirements[AUTONEW]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Requirements[EVENTS]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMORG])
- The backend asks only for a signed-in staff member — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[SESSIONONLY])

### Returns

- The new automation's id.

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/automation/automation-create-dialog/automation-create-dialog.component.ts#AutomationCreateDialogComponent.create` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#createCommunication` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: SwitchCommunication

### Summary

A staff member switches an automation on (Start) or off (Stop).

### Input

```schema
communicationId: string required ref(juicebar.communications#Communication.id)
active: boolean required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationStaff`
- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The automation is active or inactive as given — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Requirements[STARTSTOP])
- The operation is refused without `communication:role`; another organisation's automation is changed all the same — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/automation/automation-list/automation-list.component.ts#AutomationListComponent.switchState` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#switchState` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: DeleteCommunication

### Summary

A staff member deletes an automation from the list.

### Input

```schema
communicationId: string required ref(juicebar.communications#Communication.id)
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationStaff`
- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationSuperAdmin`

### Expects

- The staff member confirmed the deletion.

### Ensures

- The automation is gone — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Requirements[AUTODELETE])
- The operation is refused without `communication:role`; another organisation's automation is deleted all the same — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/automation/automation-list/automation-list.component.ts#AutomationListComponent.remove` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#deleteCommunication` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: SendCommunication

### Summary

A staff member runs an automation at once: Run in the list, or Send on the opened automation.

### Input

```schema
communicationId: string required ref(juicebar.communications#Communication.id)
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationStaff`
- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The automation runs with its content, started by the staff member — [invokes](aim:juicebar.communications#Operation:RunCommunication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Requirements[RUNNOW]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Requirements[SENDNOW]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[RUN])
- The staff member follows the run's progress, which the backend gives to any signed-in staff member — [reads](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:TaskQueue), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[SESSIONONLY])
- The operation is refused without `communication:role`, its `send` permission is not asked, and another organisation's automation runs all the same — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMORG])

### Returns

- The id of the task that carries out the run.

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/automation/automation-list/automation-list.component.ts#AutomationListComponent.run` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/recipients/automation-recipients/automation-recipients.component.ts#AutomationRecipientsComponent.send` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#sendCommunication` — as: handler
- binds: `service:communication-service#getQueue` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: UpdateCommunication

### Summary

A staff member changes an automation's name and content.

### Input

```schema
communicationId: string required ref(juicebar.communications#Communication.id)
name: string
content: string ref(juicebar.communications#Content.id)
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationStaff`
- `juicebar.communications#Persona:CommunicationSuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The automation takes the name and the content, and every other detail as the page loaded it; its recipients stay — [mutates](aim:juicebar.communications#Record:Communication), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications.automation#Requirements[AUTODETAILS])
- The operation is refused without `communication:role`; another organisation's automation is changed all the same — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.communications#Requirements[COMMORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/communications/automation/automation-details/automation-details.component.ts#AutomationDetailsComponent.save` — as: component
- binds: `service:communication-service#updateCommunication` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred
